  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Is a Low-Profile Threshold Right for My Home?",
    "text": "Is a Low-Profile Threshold Right for My Home?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Choosing the right threshold can really impact the functionality and accessibility of your entryways. A low-profile threshold is specifically designed to create a minimal step-up, making it a fantastic option if you're looking for easier passage, especially for those who might use wheelchairs or have mobility challenges. It's all about reducing that tripping hazard and creating a smoother transition between spaces.\n\nHowever, there are a few things to consider. You'll want to think about whether it will still provide an adequate seal against drafts and water—many modern low-profile thresholds are designed to do just that, but it's important to choose the right product. Also, consider how it will work with your existing door sweep, jambs, and flooring transitions. You want everything to integrate seamlessly for both function and aesthetics. When in doubt, it’s smart to get a professional opinion. HH Remodeling LLC works with homeowners throughout the Denver area, including Centennial and Aurora, and we can help you figure out if a low-profile threshold is the perfect fit for your specific needs and door system.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
